      "statement": "A simple pendulum's period depends only on its length and gravity, not on the bob's mass or small release angle. Longer rods swing slower because the bob travels a longer arc with the same restoring gravity.",
      "formula": "T = 2\\pi\\sqrt{L/g}",
      "assumptions": [
        "Small release angles (5 to 20 deg) keep the period independent of amplitude.",
        "Earth gravity is fixed at 9.81 m/s^2 with no air drag or pivot friction.",
        "The rod is massless and rigid, and the bob acts as a point mass."
      ]
